      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "2 storey detached stone farmhouse nestled high above Kilcrohane village on an elevated 0.3 acre level site enjoying panoramic sea views and across to the \r\nMizen Peninsula.   The property has a detached garage and stone outbuilding.\r\n\r\nLOCATION:\r\n\r\nThe property is located one mile from Kilcrohane village and a 30 minute drive to Bantry, the closest town.  Cork city and airport are just under a 2 hour drive from the property.  \r\n\r\nTHE ACCOMMODATION:\r\n\r\nThe property, parts of which date back to the 19th century, is in good condition and comprises:\r\n\r\nDOWNSTAIRS - 91.6 sm/986 sq.ft.\r\n\r\nreception area - (5.2m x 2.7m/17' x 9') tiled floor, coat closet\r\n\r\nopen plan kitchen/dining room - (7.3m x 3.7m/24' x 12')  sea view, slate floor, fireplace, exposed ceiling beams, door to garden\r\n\r\nliving room - (3.7m x 3.7m/12' x 12') sea view, slate floor, fireplace, exposed stone walls\r\n\r\nsunroom - (4.3m x 2.7m/14' x 9') sea view, slate floor, patio doors to outside\r\n\r\nbathroom - (3m x 2.7m/10' x9') ceramic floor tiles, shower, wash basin and WC\r\n\r\nUPSTAIRS - 51.2 sm/551 sq. ft.\r\n\r\ndouble bedroom with sea view, carpet\r\n\r\ndouble bedroom with fitted closets and sea view\r\n\r\ncloakroom with WC and wash basin, linen closet, sea view\r\n\r\nSERVICES:\r\ndeep bored well\r\nseptic tank\r\noil fired central heating\r\nelectric immersion water heater"
      },
      {
